# The GitHub CLI's updater (docs/tool-updates.md, "The GitHub CLI: a root
# recipe"). Installed as /etc/sudoers.d/termag-gh-update (0440) by
# deploy/termag-gh-update-setup.
#
# gh is root's package, so its update runs as root, in the system unit
# termag-gh-update@<run>.service. The agent user may start it, and only it,
# through the one root-owned helper, with one argument of the run id's
# alphabet (the helper checks its length): no shell, no other unit, no other
# command. The boxes' blanket NOPASSWD rule (packer/scripts/setup.sh) does
# not make this one moot: the agent never needs more than this line.
#
# The agent user is named by uid: cloud-init renames the box user at launch
# (usermod -l, uid kept). The setup script fills @AGENT_UID@ in.
#@AGENT_UID@ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/libexec/termag/termag-gh-update-start ^[a-z0-9]+$
